  "payload": {
    "rawResponseText": "When an owner of an independent upper-upscale hotel in the Caribbean and Latin America (CALA) region considers converting or affiliating their property, they typically look toward **soft brands** or **flexible conversion brands**. \n\nThese brands allow the hotel to preserve its unique name, local identity, architecture, and design while plugging into a major global hotel group’s reservation system, loyalty program, and international marketing engine.\n\nThe most commonly considered brand affiliations for independent upper-upscale property conversions in CALA include:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Major Global Soft Brands (Franchise/Management)\n\n#### **Marriott International**\nMarriott dominates the conversion landscape in CALA with two prominent upper-upscale soft brands:\n*   **Autograph Collection:** Widely regarded as a top tier choice for distinctive, boutique, or historic upper-upscale independent properties. It is heavily utilized in key CALA resort and leisure markets (including all-inclusive conversions).\n*   **Tribute Portfolio:** Designed for vibrant, lifestyle-driven upper-upscale properties. It offers lower PIP (Property Improvement Plan) entry requirements than standard hard brands, making it attractive for urban and boutique resort conversions.\n*   **Design Hotels:** Preferred by design-focused, architectural independent boutique hotels looking to leverage Marriott Bonvoy’s distribution network.\n\n#### **Hilton**\n*   **Curio Collection by Hilton:** Hilton’s primary upper-upscale conversion soft brand. Curio has expanded rapidly across Mexico, Central America, South America, and the Caribbean (including both EP resorts and all-inclusive conversions).\n*   **Tapestry Collection by Hilton:** Geared toward original, upper-upscale/upscale properties with distinct personality. It is often chosen for smaller boutique properties in urban capitals or secondary leisure destinations.\n\n#### **Hyatt Hotels Corporation**\n*   **The Unbound Collection by Hyatt:** Geared toward upper-upscale and luxury independent properties that have rich histories, unique architecture, or local significance. \n*   **JdV by Hyatt (Joie de Vivre):** A vibrant, neighborhood-centric lifestyle soft brand suitable for boutique upper-upscale urban or beach properties.\n*   **Destination by Hyatt:** A collection of independent resort and hotel properties, particularly attractive to unique leisure and golf/wellness resorts in CALA.\n\n#### **IHG Hotels & Resorts**\n*   **Vignette Collection:** IHG’s upper-upscale/luxury soft brand. It targets independent luxury and lifestyle hotels, offering rapid integration into IHG One Rewards while retaining property character.\n*   **voco hotels:** Though technically a flexible \"hard\" brand, voco is built specifically for fast, cost-effective conversions in the upper-upscale/premium space. It allows owners to maintain local design cues while adopting standardized brand touchpoints.\n\n#### **Accor**\n*   **MGallery Hotel Collection:** Accor’s upper-upscale boutique soft brand. It has a strong foothold in South America and select Caribbean markets, catering to story-led, heritage, or boutique lifestyle assets.\n*   **Handwritten Collection:** Accor's flexible midscale-to-upper-upscale collection targeting charm-filled boutique hotels.\n\n#### **Choice Hotels International**\n*   **Ascend Hotel Collection:** One of the earliest and largest soft brand networks globally. It is very popular in the Caribbean and Central America for upscale and upper-upscale historic, boutique, or resort properties seeking brand support without strict corporate standards.\n*   **Radisson Individuals:** A conversion soft brand (under Choice Hotels in the Americas) that allows independent upper-upscale properties to join Choice's network with minimal capital outlay.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Independent Consortia & Marketing Representation Networks\nFor owners who **do not** want a major brand franchise agreement (and prefer to avoid franchise fees or rigid brand requirements), non-flag marketing consortia are frequently considered:\n\n*   **Preferred Hotels & Resorts (L.V.X. or Lifestyle Collection):** Allows independent upper-upscale properties to access global GDS distribution, a global sales team, and the *I Prefer* loyalty program while maintaining 100% operational autonomy.\n*   **Small Luxury Hotels of the World (SLH):** Extremely popular for high-end boutique resort properties in the Caribbean and Latin America. Its distribution and loyalty partnership with Hilton provides massive exposure while retaining full independence.\n*   **The Leading Hotels of the World (LHW):** Primarily targets luxury assets, but top-tier landmark independent upper-upscale hotels in CALA frequently use LHW for global luxury representation.\n\n---\n\n### Key Drivers for CALA Owners When Choosing:\n1. **All-Inclusive Integration:** A huge portion of CALA hospitality growth is in all-inclusive resorts. Brands like *Autograph Collection All-Inclusive* and *Curio Collection* are heavily favored if the property is transitioning to an all-inclusive model.\n2. **Loyalty System Power:** Access to massive global guest bases (e.g., Marriott Bonvoy, Hilton Honors, World of Hyatt) is usually the primary reason owners consider affiliating.\n3. **Conversion Speed and PIP Requirements:** Conversion-focused brands like *voco*, *Tribute*, or *Ascend* generally require lower capital expenditure upfront compared to converting into a traditional \"hard brand\" (e.g., a standard Marriott, Hilton, or Westin).",
